   "source": [
    "# BT4012 · Experiment 2 V6 Extension — Application-Only and Application + LSTM Controls\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research questions**  \n",
    "**RQ1** Can a multi-source masked-attention LSTM improve standalone repayment-history prediction?  \n",
    "**RQ2** Does its out-of-fold risk score add value beyond the teammate's **All Sources** GBDT and handcrafted temporal features?  \n",
    "**RQ3** How does LSTM's incremental value vary with **observed months, number of historical loans, and installment-event density**?  \n",
    "**RQ4 (exploratory)** Can **richness-aware conditional fusion** outperform a fixed blend?\n",
    "\n",
    "**V6 changes vs V5:**  \n",
    "1. **OOF uses last-hidden pooling** (`attention=False`): V5 showed last_hidden (0.600) substantially outperformed attention (0.564) standalone; OOF now uses the stronger variant.  \n",
    "2. **Weighted BCE loss**: `pos_weight ≈ 11.5` addresses the ~8% default-rate class imbalance during LSTM training.  \n",
    "3. **Multi-source handcrafted temporal features**: `make_temporal_features` now extracts trends from bureau balance DPD, POS DPD, and credit card utilisation channels (8 → 14 features).  \n",
    "4. **Bureau balance flat aggregates** added to GBDT feature set: `bb_max_dpd`, `bb_months_with_dpd`, `bb_ever_late_share`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run top to bottom in Colab with GPU. All data live in `MyDrive/home_credit_bt4012/clean_data`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Added controlled comparison (V6 extension):** V6 already includes `M_app` (application-only GBDT). This notebook additionally evaluates **`M_app_LSTM`**, the *same* application-only features plus the *same existing* out-of-fold LSTM score used by M2/M3. This isolates the incremental value of LSTM-derived history when historical aggregates are absent, versus when they are present (`M2 - M0`). All original models and splits are retained.\n"
   ]
  },
