    "## 3 · Build multi-source monthly sequences (oldest → newest)\n",
    "\n",
    "**V5:** The monthly tensor now fuses four data sources into a single timeline per customer:\n",
    "- **Installments** (13 channels): DPD, late rate, payment ratio, loan-aware dispersion — same as V4.\n",
    "- **Bureau balance** (5 channels): monthly DPD status of loans at *other* lenders — **new, previously unused**.\n",
    "- **POS cash** (3 channels): monthly DPD and remaining obligations on POS/cash loans — **new for sequences**.\n",
    "- **Credit card** (3 channels): monthly utilization, DPD, payment-to-minimum ratio — **new for sequences**.\n",
    "\n",
    "All sources share the same 12-month window (`T=12`). Bureau balance and POS/credit-card tables use `MONTHS_BALANCE` directly; installments are mapped via `floor(-DAYS_INSTALMENT / 30)`. Customers with no records from any source get all-zero rows (observed mask = False)."
   ]
