   "source": [
    "### Interpretation checklist\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Larger positive uplift for `M_app_LSTM − M_app`, but near-zero `M2 − M0`:** compatible with historical aggregates already capturing some predictive signal available in the LSTM score. Not conclusive proof of information redundancy.\n",
    "- **Both near zero:** the scalar LSTM score may be weak, redundant, or poorly fused even without aggregates.\n",
    "- **Both positive:** the LSTM score may add useful signal under both feature sets.\n",
    "- **Negative uplift:** adding the LSTM score can harm generalization; retain and report this result.\n",
    "\n",
    "Check both ROC-AUC and PR-AUC; use the paired bootstrap intervals rather than point estimates alone. No test-set evaluation or retuning is performed here.\n"
   ]
  },
