   "source": [
    "## 11 · Richness-aware fusion (exploratory, disjoint calibration/evaluation)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why:** A customer with no repayment history cannot provide a meaningful individualized LSTM sequence; sparse and dense histories may warrant different weighting. We compare three ways of combining the **already-fitted M1 GBDT** and the **OOF-trained LSTM ensemble**:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **M1 only**: no LSTM score.\n",
    "- **Fixed blend**: one learned global weight, fitted on calibration-only data.\n",
    "- **Richness-aware blend**: a small regularized logistic model using *logit(M1), logit(LSTM), three log-scaled richness measures, and score x richness interactions*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important:** The M1 GBDT and LSTM are trained on `train`, not `val`. We split `val` into `calibration` and `evaluation` (stratified). Blend parameters are selected on calibration only; evaluation is disjoint. This reduces evaluation sample size and is **not** directly comparable with full-validation M0-M3 results."
   ]
  },
