    "## 13 · Interpretation guide\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **First verify M0 parity** against the teammate's All Sources run. Matching model parameters alone does not guarantee identical features/preprocessing.\n",
    "2. **Primary result**: M3 vs M1 on full validation. If LSTM hurts, report it.\n",
    "3. **Richness**: report sample counts, positives, subgroup default rates, and AUC deltas for coverage, loan breadth and density. Do not infer a monotonic benefit without evidence.\n",
    "4. **Conditional fusion**: compare methods on the **same held-out evaluation half** only. Calibration AUC is optimistic and is not the headline metric.\n",
    "5. **Leakage audit**: cleaned installment rows may include future payment totals for installments due before application. Verify `installments.parquet` construction and payment-time availability before interpreting results as deployable. For strict point-in-time correctness, reconstruct from payment events with timestamps and censor payments after application date.\n",
    "6. **Test**: keep locked until model and calibration choices are frozen. For a gated model, final test scoring requires constructing test richness features, score predictions and applying a frozen gate; the existing optional test cell below covers M0–M3 only."
   ]
