    "## Interpretation and limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Additive chain design:** M_app -> M0 -> M1 -> M2 -> M3. Each step adds exactly one ingredient on top of M0 (the Exp 1 baseline), isolating its marginal contribution.\n",
    "- **Primary claim:** incremental validation performance of M1 and M2 over M0, and whether the full M3 exceeds either alone.\n",
    "- **V6 improvements:** weighted BCE loss, last-hidden OOF pooling, 14 multi-source handcrafted temporal features, bureau balance flat aggregates in GBDT.\n",
    "- **M_app baseline:** Shows the value of all historical data; the gap M_app -> M0 is the historical contribution to the GBDT.\n",
    "- **If no lift:** report that the tested LSTM representation was not complementary; avoid cherry-picking a favorable seed.\n",
    "- **Baseline parity:** compare M0 to your teammate's Exp 1 output. Same hyperparameters are necessary but not sufficient.\n",
    "- **OOF caveat:** training scores come from fold models, while val/test scores are multi-model averages; their noise levels differ.\n",
    "- **Leakage audit:** cleaned installment rows may include future payment totals. Bureau balance uses `MONTHS_BALANCE` which is relative to application, so no temporal leakage.\n",
    "- **Compute:** the notebook trains 3 OOF LSTMs (2-layer, hidden=64) plus standalone/ablation models; GPU recommended."
   ]
  },
