    "## 15 · Multi-model fusion — segment-aware ensemble\n",
    "\n",
    "**Motivation:** Individual models M0–M3 show small, overlapping differences on the test set. Rather than selecting a single best model, we explore whether combining their predictions can reduce variance and improve robustness. Three strategies are compared:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Validation-AUC weighted average** of M0–M3: each model's weight is proportional to its validation ROC-AUC.\n",
    "2. **Pairwise blend (M0+M2):** grid-search the optimal mixing weight on validation.\n",
    "3. **Stacking meta-learner:** a regularized logistic regression on logit-transformed model scores, segment indicators, richness features, and score×richness interactions, fitted on a calibration half of the validation set.\n",
    "\n",
    "All fusion weights are selected on validation only; test-set predictions are generated once."
   ]
